    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "REA Eoin Dillon are pleased to present to the market this charming three/four bed bungalow in the scenic setting of Coolbawn, County Tipperary. The tranquil lakeside location of this bungalow is sure to impress the most discerning purchaser, offering peace and serenity in this idyllic hideaway. \nUpon entering the property, you are welcomed by a bright porch with tiled flooring, leading into the main hallway, which is finished with carpet flooring and provides a seamless flow throughout the home. To the right, the cosy sitting room features carpet flooring and an open fireplace, creating a warm and inviting atmosphere. The dining room, also carpeted, leads through to the kitchen and adjoining living room. The kitchen is fitted with tiled flooring and an electric oven and hob, while also providing access to the utility room. The utility room is fully tiled and plumbed for a washing machine, dryer, and dishwasher. The spacious living room features carpet flooring and opens into a glass roof sunroom, which provides direct access to the rear gardens and allows for an abundance of natural light.\nThe property comprises three well proportioned bedrooms, all finished with carpet flooring, with one bedroom further benefiting from a fully tiled en-suite bathroom. Completing the accommodation is the fully tiled family bathroom, fitted with a W.C., W.H.B., and bath with overhead shower.\nExternally, the property is set on beautifully landscaped grounds and enjoys scenic views overlooking the stunning Lough Derg. To the rear of the garden, there is a substantial three-bay haybarn with stable extending to approximately 103.96 sq.m.\n\nSkehana, Coolbawn provides access to Lough Derg, a majestic lake located between the counties of Clare, Tipperary and Galway where you will find activities to keep you entertained; sailing, canoeing, fishing and magnificent scenery.\n\nViewing by appointment only. \n\nEntrance porch - 1.67m (5'6) x 1.47m (4'10)\nTiled floor\n\nHallway - 4.03m (13'3) x 1.47m (4'10)\nCarpet floor\n\nSitting room - 4.18m (13'9) x 3.65m (12'0)\nCarpet floor with an open fireplace\n\nDining room - 5.33m (17'6) x 3.36m (11'0)\nCarpet floor\n\nLiving Room - 4.53m (14'10) x 3.54m (11'7)\nCarpet floor\n\nSunroom - 3.58m (11'9) x 1.77m (5'10)\nTile floor and glass roof\n\nKitchen - 3.77m (12'4) x 1.69m (5'7)\nTile floor, electric oven and hob\n\nUtility - 2.92m (9'7) x 2.59m (8'6)\nTile floor, plumbed for washing machine, dryer and dishwasher.\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.02m (9'11) x 2.61m (8'7)\nCarpet floor\n\nFamily bathroom - 2.59m (8'6) x 2.31m (7'7)\nLino flooring, W.C, W.H.B and bath with overhead shower\n\nBedroom 2 - 4.35m (14'3) x 2.59m (8'6)\nCarpet flooring, built in wardrobes and W.H.B\n\nMaster bedroom - 5.07m (16'8) x 3.25m (10'8)\nCarpet flooring and built in wardrobes\n\nEn-suite - 3.25m (10'8) x 2.04m (6'8)\nTile flooring, W.C, W.H.B and shower\n\nBedroom 4/Study - 4.17m (13'8) x 3.14m (10'4)\nCarpet floor and built in wardrobes\n\n\nDirections\nFrom Nenagh take the main Borrisokane road ( N52). Take the 2nd exit at the roundabout heading for Borrisokane. Take a slight left onto R493, heading towards Knigh. Continue for approximately 10km. Then turn left towards Coolbawn and continue for 1.9km. Turn right onto Annagh road. Continue onto Lahesseragh and then onto L1101 Skehanagh and the property will be located on your right identified by our For Sale sign. Eircode: E45 TX48\n\nwhat3words /// salaried.sweaters.sweatshirt\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
